{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7840448","formula":"Br₃HSi","hill":"Br3HSi","elements":["H","Si","Br"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"Br":3.0,"Si":1.0},"names":{"en":"Tribromosilane","ru":"Трибромсилан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tribromosilane is the chemical compound with the formula HBr3Si. At high temperatures, it decomposes to produce silicon, and is an alternative to purified trichlorosilane of ultrapure silicon in the semiconductor industry. The Schumacher Process of silicon deposition uses tribromosilane gas to produce polysilicon, but it has a number of cost and safety advantages over the Siemens Process to make polysilicon.","ru":"Трибромсилан — неорганическое соединение, бромпроизводное моносилана с формулой SiHBr3, бесцветная жидкость, реагирует с водой, самовоспламеняется на воздухе."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":82244,"mass":268.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"[SiH](Br)(Br)Br","inchikey":"IBOKZQNMFSHYNQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"tribromosilane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"82244","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.04,"y":0.382,"z":0.185,"el":"Br"},{"x":1.351,"y":1.575,"z":0.185,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.689,"y":-1.957,"z":0.185,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-0.556,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-2.041,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[1,3,1],[2,3,1],[3,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7840448","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribromosilane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/8